  "artifact_identity": "Root owns frozen scoped artifact and exact deltas. Five changed files among six owned; accounts.test.ts unchanged. Primary production source, claims harness and schema are final. Sole post-primary change is the route-test arrival sequencing/type refinement retained below; independent frozen routes+claims execution is required.",
  "implementation": [
    "AccountStore production API has no unconditional full-account put, remove or session writer. Create-only insertion refuses id/email conflicts. Fixture-only memory setup retains put/remove/putSession.",
    "Conditional D1 account predicates compare id/email/password hash/roles/permissions/onboarding/disabled plus updated_at. Login only writes last-sign-in metadata and one session; unchanged authority permits independent simultaneous logins.",
    "Prepared JWT pairs precede persistence. Password batch conditionally inserts a fresh session with live source sid/current enabled account, revokes other sessions while the old account predicate holds, then changes only password/onboarding/revision. A reused JTI aborts even if the account/source precondition is stale, preventing an earlier session from authorizing dependent writes.",
    "Admin field-specific patch/reset/delete and affected-session revocation share a native D1 batch. Security changes and logout advance updated_at monotonically with MAX(previous+1,now); logout deletes sessions in that batch. Memory methods mirror conditional mutation/revocation semantics.",
    "Stale conditional mutations return409 without tokens or success audit. Account migration is create-only then conditional first sign-in; failed first-session commit can leave a recoverable inserted D1 account. KV cleanup and migration/sign-in audit follow successful session commit.",
    "Existing login admission/body/dummy work, restricted recovery, human/service distinctions, enforced global admin withdrawal and tenant/shopper/core/learning paths retained. Kit documents conflict/relogin and migration/commit limitations."
